          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"is to his mate. In order to secure the elephant, there must be\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"a strong post (\u0906\u0932\u093e\u0928 ); and to curb a sensual mind a strong\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"control or restraint. The post and the restraint, the elephant\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"and the mind and the sensual objects and the female elephant,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"are the pairs compared here. \u0924\u093e\u0926\u0943\u0915\u094d\u2014a worldly man who is\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"strong minded enough to resist the temptation of sensual\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"objects. \u0915\u094d\u0937\u0940\u092c\u2014intoxicated. \u0906\u0932\u093e\u0928 a post for fastening elephants.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 83. \u0905\u0915\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092a\u0923\u094d\u092f\u2014cf. \u0915\u0943\u092a\u0923\u093e\u0902 \u0935\u0943\u0924\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0902 Nit. sl. 49. \u0909\u092a\u0936\u092e\u2014tranquil-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"lity, or peace of mind, subduing the passions entirely. \u092c\u0939\u093f\u0903\",\"end\":\"join\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u092e\u0928\u094d\u0926\u0938\u094d\u092a\u0928\u094d\u0926\u092e\u094d\u2014(the mind too), moving ( but ) slowly towards\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"external objects. The mind is solely engaged in contemplation\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"and hardly bestows any thought on external objects. The\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"internal objects for a contemplative mind are itself and the\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"supreme soul; while the entire creation constitutes outer\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"things. These latter are referred to by the word \u092c\u0939\u093f\u0903.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit text is difficult to read.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 84. \u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u0923\u093e\u0903\u2014have died out. Cf. \u091c\u0940\u0930\u094d\u0923\u092e\u0919\u094d\u0917\u0947 \u0938\u0941\u092d\u093e\u0937\u093f\u0924\u092e\u094d Sl. 2.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u0935\u0928\u094d\u0927\u094d\u092f\u092b\u0932\u0924\u093e\u0902 \u092f\u093e\u0924\u093e\u0903\u2014have become sterile, have borne no fruit.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0915\u0943\u0924\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0903-see com.; or \u0915\u0943\u0924\u0902 \u0905\u0928\u094d\u0924\u092f\u0924\u0940\u0924\u093f. \u0905\u0915\u094d\u0937\u092e\u093f\u2014unforgiving, unrelent-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"ing; \u0915\u094d\u0937\u092e\u093e \u0935\u093f\u0926\u094d\u092f\u0924\u0947 \u0905\u0938\u094d\u092f \u0915\u094d\u0937\u092e\u0940 \u0928 \u0915\u094d\u0937\u092e\u0940 \u0905\u0915\u094d\u0937\u092e\u093f. \u0906\u0939\u093e\u0924\u0941\u092e\u094d\u2013v. l.=\u0939\u093f + \u0906 +\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u0939\u093e\u0924\u0941\u092e\u094d, \u0906 being taken \u0938\u094d\u092e\u0930\u0923\u0947 as Mr. Talang suggests. But here\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"\u0939\u093f has no propriety.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Several Sanskrit words, especially the variant in lines 4\u20135, are unclear.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 85. \u092e\u0947 \u092d\u0947\u0926\u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u093f\u092a\u0924\u094d\u0924\u093f\u0930\u094d\u0928\u093e\u0938\u094d\u0924\u093f\u2014I see no difference; I have no\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"idea of difference between &c. \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0924\u093f\u092a\u0924\u094d\u0924\u093f\u2014knowledge, idea.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u091c\u0917\u0924\u093e\u092e\u094d\u2014the plural is used because according to the Hindu\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"notion there are 14 worlds.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 86. \u092a\u0941\u0932\u093f\u0928\u0947\u2014\u0924\u094b\u092f\u094b\u0924\u094d\u0925\u093f\u0924\u0902 \u0924\u0924\u094d\u092a\u0941\u0932\u093f\u0928\u0902 Amara; a sandy bank left\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"by receding water; goes with \u0938\u0941\u0930\u0938\u0930\u093f\u0924\u0903. \u0938\u0941\u0930\u0938\u0930\u093f\u0924\u094d\u2014the heavenly river,\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"the Ganges. \u092d\u0935\u092d\u094b\u0917\u094b\u0926\u094d\u0935\u093f\u0917\u094d\u0928\u093e\u0903\u2014\u092c\u0939\u0941\u0926\u0941\u0903\u0916\u091c\u0928\u094d\u092e\u092a\u0930\u0902\u092a\u0930\u093e\u092d\u0940\u0924\u093e\u0903 R\u00e1marshi; cf.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u092d\u094d\u0930\u092e\u0938\u0941\u0916\u092d\u094b\u0917 sl. 96 infra. \u0906\u0924\u094d\u0924\u0935\u091a\u0938\u0903 v. l.\u2014\u0906\u0924\u094d\u0924\u0902 \u0917\u0943\u0939\u0940\u0924\u0902 \u0935\u091a\u0903 \u092f\u0948\u0903 \u0924\u0947;\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"who have taken to ( i. e. are repeating ) the words. \u0906\u0928\u0928\u094d\u0926\u094b\u0926\u094d\u092d\u0942\u0924\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"&c.\u2014Bah. The joy referred to is, of course, that resulting\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"from the manifestation of the Supreme Deity in contempla-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"tion. \u0906\u0930\u094d\u0924\u0935\u091a\u0938\u0903 v. l. is meaningless unless we take it to mean\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"\u2018 earnest cries, fervent prayers,\u2019 ( \u0906\u0930\u094d\u0924\u0938\u094d\u092f \u0907\u0935 \u0935\u091a\u0903 \u092f\u0947\u0937\u093e\u0902 ).\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit quotations are indistinct.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 74 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\",\"u6\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"82\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"83\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"84\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"85\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u6\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"86\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r6\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]}],\"relations\":[]}"
